# Behind Caddy there is deliberately no HTTP-to-HTTPS redirect server here.
# Caddy redirects plain-HTTP visitors itself, before nginx is involved, and
# every request that reaches nginx is plain HTTP by design — a redirect on 80
# would send each one back to https, which Caddy would forward to 80 again,
# forever.
#
# What this file does instead is about the redirects nginx makes by itself
# (the /26BR -> /26BR/ rewrites, a directory asked for without its trailing
# slash). nginx builds their Location from its own scheme, which here is
# http://, so a visitor on https would be sent to http. absolute_redirect off
# makes it send just the path ("Location: /26BR/"), and the browser resolves
# that against the https URL it is already on.
#
# Set here, at http level (00-redirect.conf includes this file outside any
# server block), so that every server inherits it. A server block may still
# say the same thing itself: baja-app-certificado does, in every mode.
absolute_redirect off;
